on this union of intervals."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ad95b4e-e367-5e26-800c-1a87a537ca83" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals on Which a Trigonometric Function Is Continuous"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da51e3ef-d19b-5cf9-8c44-a976268bbbe0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284205} {:answer/id #uuid "ad2369b9-93e6-54b2-bacf-60c3bc26fa94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284206} {:answer/id #uuid "a91d7bf9-9db9-5d2e-8427-9356994814ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284207} {:answer/id #uuid "302c5071-5bb0-5a26-aa2d-740b369ac9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284208} {:answer/id #uuid "30de9e0a-dbcb-591f-9341-36cfd26277bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-\\frac{1}{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad2369b9-93e6-54b2-bacf-60c3bc26fa94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284206} :answer-field/id #uuid "a409d73e-0475-5491-9501-58ba11de9964" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284204}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "72c4a1b6-b529-582d-ae56-b36a4ca3015a" :question/math-academy-id "q-39769" :question/problem "Find the largest interval on which the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2x+1})$ is continuous." :question/worked-solution "The function is a composition of two functions, a radical function, and a cosine function.\n\nThe cosine is continuous at all points in its domain, and its domain consists of all real numbers. So, we focus on the radical function.\n\nLikewise, the radical function $\\sqrt{2x+1}$ is continuous at all points in its domain. To find its domain, we set the expression under the radical to be greater than or equal to zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1\\ge 0\\,⟹\\,2x\\ge -1\\,⟹\\,x\\ge -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)$ is $[-\\frac{1}{2},\\infty )$, and the function is continuous on this interval."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c9958ee-c8b0-5d33-8755-e61cb445b0de" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals on Which a Logarithmic Function Is Continuous"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ca56486-6df5-5cc0-a2bd-953bd1370544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284212} {:answer/id #uuid "b2367b65-5462-52a2-96fd-e0ab3fa26e61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284213} {:answer/id #uuid "f0e91445-f8a9-5fca-83ff-295866127fc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284214} {:answer/id #uuid "530715af-d9c3-5629-b681-cbd0b8fbda95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-\\infty ,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284215} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9cfe74-75ef-51fa-b1b8-f231376b4967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ca56486-6df5-5cc0-a2bd-953bd1370544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284212} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6330345-8d8c-52c8-be38-0d950db1e6cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96948c86-86f8-5380-b7ba-c08d3c3e11b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-76072" :question/problem "Find the largest interval of continuity for the function $f(x)={log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{{5}^{x}}).$" :question/worked-solution "Our function is a logarithmic function, so it is continuous over all points in its domain.\n\nTo find the domain of ${log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{{5}^{x}}),$ we set the expression under the logarithm to be greater than zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-2}{{5}^{x}}>0\\,⟹\\,x-2>0\\,⟹\\,x>2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $f(x)={log}_{3}⁡(\\frac{x-2}{{5}^{x}})$ is $(2,\\infty ),$ and it is also continuous on this interval."}]}
